# --- editors and OS cruft ---
# .vscode/settings.json was tracked until now. Its contents were personal prefs (a
# language-server choice, a Postman notification toggle) — nothing a collaborator
# needs, and the kind of file that produces merge conflicts over nobody's setting.
# Un-ignore a specific file (e.g. !.vscode/extensions.json) if shared config is ever
# genuinely wanted.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
lab
/assets/
alembic.ini

# --- private working notes ---
# Operational runbook and planning docs. Not committed: the README carries what a
# reviewer needs, while these carry local specifics and what is still missing.
RUNBOOK.md
FINAL_PROJECT_PLAN.md
AI_HANDOFF.md
notes/

# --- evaluation run artifacts ---
# Per-run output, not deliverables. `reports/experiments/` alone is ~5MB of saved
# answers that exist so an interrupted sweep can resume, and every RAGAS run drops
# another timestamped report. The ones worth keeping get stable names
# (reports/ragas_latest.json, reports/mlflow_comparison.png) and stay tracked.
reports/experiments/
reports/ragas_*T*Z.json
reports/sweep_*.log
